From 812b077fe307da5182676778c422ed8f761a67be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fujii Hironori <fujii@igalia.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:03:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [WPE] Give the headless WPEPlatform display a virtual
 1920x1080 screen

The headless display had no screen, so WebCore fell back to the view
bounds as the screen rectangle, and LocalDOMWindow::adjustWindowRect()
clamped every window.resizeTo()/resizeBy() request to the current view
size. The toplevel was never resized and no resize event was ever
dispatched, so the tests waiting for one timed out in WebKitTestRunner.

Add a 1920x1080 virtual screen (about 96 DPI, 60 Hz, without a sync
observer, so the display link still uses the timer) to the headless
display and return it from the headless toplevel.

* LayoutTests/platform/wpe/TestExpectations: Remove the expectations of
the tests that now pass.
* Source/WebKit/WPEPlatform/wpe/headless/WPEDisplayHeadless.cpp:
(wpe_screen_headless_class_init): Return no sync observer, so that
DisplayVBlankMonitorWPE is not created and does not open a DRM device.
(wpeDisplayHeadlessConnect):
(wpeDisplayHeadlessGetNScreens):
(wpeDisplayHeadlessGetScreen):
(wpe_display_headless_class_init):
* Source/WebKit/WPEPlatform/wpe/headless/WPEToplevelHeadless.cpp:
(wpeToplevelHeadlessGetScreen):
(wpe_toplevel_headless_class_init):
